Why do they use those two cards?

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.910
Well, because...

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.950
I can understand "The fall paddy shacks,"

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.410
since Emperor Tenji wrote it and 
he's enshrined at Omi Jingu.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:46.570
Yeah, and "May the scarlet..."

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:51.470
The first characters in its first and second 
verse form "meijin," the word for "Master."

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.120
<b>Mei</b>

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:49.120
<b>Jin</b>

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.880
<b>Master</b>

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.300
That's a good omen!

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.120
It's just some silly wordplay!

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.470
Then what do they use in 
the Queen match?

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.970
<i>Councilor Sei</i>

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.470
<i>Lady Murasaki</i>

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.470
<b>Ohhhh!   Ahh, right 
Makes sense now   Okay!   That's easy to understand 
I get it   Uh-huh, uh-huh   Ooooh   Huh 
