00:04:49.560 --> 00:05:02.400
Large cards with the unique syllables on them are set up on display boards to make it easier for the audience to follow what's happening in the match. 
They're added, removed, and relocated as the match plays out. Friends or younger members of the competitors' karuta societies are usually asked to do it.

