You could tell?</b>

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.740
<i>I'm going to play until I win, Suo-kun!</i>

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.850
<i>This one might be...</i>

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.590
<i>a little difficult.</i>

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.120
<i>None are left...</i>

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:30.140
<i>Since the dew atop the blades...</i>

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.930
It's back and forth between 
Wakamiya and Inokuma.

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:35.340
Neither is giving an inch.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:37.110
The crowd seems to be buzzing.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:41.060
Do you know how they're able to play 
such an evenly-matched game, Uotani-san?

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:42.500
It's Uozumi.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:43.930
How is that, Watarai-san?

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.870
Because they're playing 
karuta their own way.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:47.340
Huh?

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:50.520
Haruka-chan is more than just a challenger.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.440
She's been Queen four times.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:57.570
<i>I was sure Wakamiya would 
have the advantage, but...</i>

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.360
<i>There's no telling now.</i>

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:03.300
It's said that the air at Omi Jingu
weakens challengers

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:07.040
and gives strength to the Master and Queen,

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:07.860
but look.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.470
Which one has the eyes that say,
"I'm the Queen"?

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:14.120
Her eyes are huge! 
Shinobu-chan's eyes look so intimidating! 
Those intense eyes...   Mommy! 
Haruka-chan lol

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:17.350
<i>They're both keeping a tight 
defense on their own side.</i>

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:19.830
<i>The crucial point will be when one 
of them goes for the other's side.</i>

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:21.800
<i>I would go on the attack.</i>

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.510
<i>But could I even do that?</i>

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.010
<i>Inokuma-san's placement makes 
her cards hard to take.</i>

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.150
<i>So spring nights...</i>

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:30.980
<i>She attacked!</i>

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.250
<i>She got one from Inokuma's side!</i>

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.170
<i>The sky may hold...</i>

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:38.090
<i>Inokuma-san's defense has been 
so strong. What happened?</i>

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.610
<i>Shinobu-chan is farther 
away, but she was faster.</i>

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:45.740
<i>In a match as close as this, 
even a few centimeters matter.</i>

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:50.240
<i>They both listen closely and accelerate 
their hands to take cards.</i>

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:53.230
<i>The hand that has farther to 
travel can accelerate more.</i>

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:57.150
<i>Haruka-san is faster at taking cards
on her outside.</i>

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:01.430
<i>She loses the cards on her inside
to Wakamiya-san.</i>

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:05.000
<i>Does her placement really 
make cards harder to take?</i>

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.150
<i>As friends and strangers...</i>

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:11.270
<i>they all exchange hellos and goodbyes 
at the famous gates of Afusaka</i>

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:10.340
<i>I just need to bring the monks home, 
even if I get a little rough.</i>

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:11.260
<i>And...</i>

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.330
<i>Rain takes longer...</i>

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:22.990
<i>leaving a hovering mist 
above the trees and grass</i>

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.710
<i>No matter how much 
Inokuma-san has practiced</i>

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.130
<i>to get closer to her personal prime,</i>

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:22.970
<i>nothing she can do will help her take a 
one-syllable card from the young Queen.</i>

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:26.120
<i>She's fast.</i>

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:28.630
<i>Wakamiya-san really is good.</i>

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:29.830
<i>I can't get past her.</i>

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:31.360
<i>But...</i>

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:36.260
<i>Impassionate gods have never seen</i>

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.250
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:38.440
One of Inokuma-san's best cards!

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:40.240
And we saw her fist clench in victory!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.330
<i>Seriously? This is pissing me off.</i>

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.720
<i>There are too many players who 
wig out over "Impassionate."</i>

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.690
<i>Too many...</i>

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.150
As you said, Watarai-san,

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:57.940
the goddess of victory couldn't 
make a call until the very end.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.530
It's come down to luck of the draw.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:03.690
This is Wakamiya-san's first 
luck-of-the-draw in an official match.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.810
How's this going to end? 
Who will Lady Luck smile upon?

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:09.310
<i>"How will it end"?</i>

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:11.620
<i>Since I could not hide...</i>

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.070
<i>There's no chance these cards...</i>

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.590
<i>wouldn't choose me.</i>

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.330
<i>people would always ask if 
I was pining for someone</i>

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:19.960
The Queen wins the first match!

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.640
But she was forced into a luck-of-the-draw.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:25.590
There's still no telling what'll 
happen in the remaining matches.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.090
<i>Shinobu-chan and Inokuma-san 
both played well.</i>

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:30.140
<i>How would I have played that match?</i>

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:31.710
<i>How would I...</i>

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:34.390
<i>What about Dr. Harada?</i>

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:35.700
<i>Nasty!</i>

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:36.880
<i>Nasty!</i>

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:38.910
<i>He's nasty! And stupid, too!</i>

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.020
<i>That idiot!</i>

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:41.270
<i>No way...</i>

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:43.270
<i>It's luck of the draw there, too?!</i>

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.230
<i>Look</i>

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.230
<i>May the scarlet</i>

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:50.160
<i>May the scarlet kadsuras 
of Mount Afusaka...</i>

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.550
The Master match is also settled 
with a luck-of-the-draw!

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:57.130
But the winner here is the 
challenger, Harada, grade 6.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.600
Master Suo's record of 
consecutive wins ends at 12

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:03.240
as his 57-year-old challenger 
scores the first win!

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:04.830
I expected no less.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.370
When you end up in a luck-of-the-draw,

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:09.340
your card is always the one read.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:12.100
What are you trying to pull?

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:18.510
<i>Suo-kun's tasteless humor 
just backfired on him.</i>

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:22.460
<i>He was trying to end with the same card 
differential as the Queen match,</i>

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:24.900
<i>but who knew it would end 
in a luck-of-the-draw?</i>

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:29.910
<i>Even Suo-san can't predict which card 
will be read in a luck-of-the-draw.</i>

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:33.650
<i>I bet he never expected to lose, though.</i>

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.610
<i>Serves him right!</i>

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.090
<i>No...</i>

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:39.670
<i>That's not it... Dr. Harada...</i>

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.530
<i>Dr. Harada, Suo-san...</i>

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:48.930
Nothing. When I realized 
this might be the last time,

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.550
I just wanted to sit here longer.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:54.420
<i>He's planning to control 
even the number of wins</i>

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.400
<i>so he can drag this out to five matches!</i>

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:04.010
The second match will begin 
after lunch, at 12:45 PM.

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:06.190
Your numbered tickets will be...

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.860
Challenger
Harada Hideo's
Green Room

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:09.790
Check out Dr. Harada.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:12.010
He's got so many people rooting for him.

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.440
So where is he?

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.950
Recovering from his fatigue, as usual.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.130
Want to talk to him?

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:22.240
Nah, that's okay.

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:24.330
I'm gonna check out somewhere else.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.950
What was it again?

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.290
Master
Suo Hisashi's
Green Room

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:27.440
I think it was in Harajuku...

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:30.340
Suo-san's more popular than you'd think.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:33.460
Being around Suo-san means 
sweets are always close by!

00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:36.310
You're nicer than people 
think too, Sudo-kun.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:37.360
Card boy!

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:38.340
I am not!

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:40.260
I'll be here as the challenger next year!

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:44.280
What? You got into the Nico stream, 
but it kicked you out?

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:47.180
There's a premium membership?

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.990
Pre... P...

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:51.270
Forget it.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:54.280
Challenger
Inokuma Haruka's
Green Room

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:55.460
You know, Jin, we need to 
start weaning you soon.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.660
Mommy, you have to win the next game!

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.860
Eat a rice ball!

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.440
Mommy sure is tough.

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:03.180
Oh, I need to change your diaper!

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.020
I'll do that...

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.240
Eat it! Eat it!

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:08.990
Thanks, Aki.

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:14.380
Hello.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:17.390
Rion? I thought you weren't going to come.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.280
Rion-chan! You came all this way?

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:21.390
Well, um...

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:26.290
My grandma's reading at the Prince 
Takamatsu Memorial Cup tomorrow, so...

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.270
<b>She'll be doing some
commentating, too</b>

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:27.280
And you're playing?

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.410
Impressive! You've got a lot of drive.

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:30.960
Oh, n-not really...

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.390
I need to work hard, too.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.650
If Makoto knew you were playing in 
the Prince Takamatsu Memorial Cup,

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:38.230
I bet he'd be here, too.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:38.890
Huh?

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.960
Oh, I doubt that.

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.060
He has his center exam next week.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:47.120
I didn't tell anyone I was coming here 
for the Prince Takamatsu Memorial Cup.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.300
I just stopped by on the way...

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:51.020
But you were amazing, Haruka-san!

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:54.030
The first match was great, 
and I'm sure the second...

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:55.050
Rion-chan.

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:58.340
Watch me, okay?

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:01.690
Watch closely.

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:07.870
Because this will probably be 
my last Queen match.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:14.110
Queen
Wakamiya Shinobu's
Green Room

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:18.180
I know it's nothing new,

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.740
but it sure is quiet in h—

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:24.060
<i>That was so interesting...</i>

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.740
<i>So interesting...</i>

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:28.500
<i>Even that weird placement...</i>

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.580
<i>Next time, I'll do this.</i>

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.200
Don't swing when you're holding chopsticks!

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:32.960
<i>I'll bring them home this way.</i>

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.760
<i>That placement may be 
incomprehensible to most,</i>

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:37.830
<i>but it's interesting.</i>

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:42.380
<i>It's a chance to see just how 
connected I am to the cards.</i>

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:46.500
<i>She's interesting... and strong.</i>

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:48.230
<i>And fun!</i>

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:51.420
Oh, look! What did I tell you?

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:54.120
Stop doing swings with 
those long sleeves on!

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:56.010
I'm sorry.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:59.060
A kimono with long sleeves...

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:01.780
Mom really doesn't understand 
karuta at all.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:04.130
I hope that doesn't stain.

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:06.290
I'll have to talk to the maker later...

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.310
And you were awfully obedient 
about wearing it.

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:10.920
It doesn't bother me.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.320
I'm good, anyway.

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:14.110
And you need to be.

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:15.790
Hidakaya-san is watching, you know.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:19.880
The Kyoto Textile Association that 
Hidakaya-san is the chairman of

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:22.170
is one of Mom's valuable constituents.

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:24.610
What?

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:26.450
What's that look for?

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:30.450
You know she wouldn't buy her granddaughter
a fancy kimono like that just to show support.

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:34.690
She's a politician, and you're 
an attractive advertisement.

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:45.530
Excuse me.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.230
Who might you be?

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:48.800
Oh, I'm here...

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:51.530
as support for Shinobu-chan, 
sort of. I brought a gift.

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:53.520
Chihaya, sit!

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.340
<i>"Chihaya"?</i>

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:55.870
Uh... Th-Thanks.

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.900
You came all the way from Tokyo?
Must have a lot of time on your hands.

00:19:56.800 --> 00:20:02.380
<b>Here</b>

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:02.370
Dr. Harada is my karuta coach.

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:04.360
Shouldn't you be giving 
<i>him</i> your support, then?!

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.320
Huh? But I couldn't help it!

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:08.890
Dr. Harada has my total support,

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:12.390
but you and Inokuma-san are both my rivals!

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:13.150
Huh?

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:16.820
You couldn't even win the East Japan qualifier,
and you call yourself my rival?

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.150
<i>Is she a friend?</i>

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:19.910
<i>Shinobu's actually talking to her 
without saying anything mean.</i>

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:19.460
So, what? You don't want 
any Snowmaru dorayaki?

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:19.910
I do!

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:21.350
I'm having one!

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:26.120
Let's play karuta again!

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:27.800
When?

00:20:29.190 --> 00:20:30.610
The Queen match!

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:34.280
I wanted to win and come 
here as the challenger,

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:37.250
but the East Japan qualifier was 
on the same day as my class trip.

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:44.890
Oh, also, my friend and I were talking...

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:47.250
It might be easier to 
play if you use tasuki.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.400
Tasuki?

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:52.580
She has long sleeves. 
That would look sloppy.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:53.520
<b>We don't have tasuki, anyway</b>

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:53.520
But...

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:55.260
A class trip?

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:05.330
It's time.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:07.710
Competitors, please assemble 
in the Urayasu room.

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:18.740
Honestly, that girl!
What a terrible attitude!

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:21.170
But she does have a match 
to play. Forgive her.
